                <head>Annex 33</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Statement by the United States
                        Delegation on Annex 7—Part 4—Miscellaneous</hi></p>
                <p>The U. S. opposes the U.K. proposals regarding stock exchange and commercial
                    exchange contracts and the sale of securities for unpaid debts. These highly
                    specialized provisions do not appear necessary or suitable for inclusion in a
                    general peace treaty. The U. S. particularly questions the desirability of a
                    multilateral peace treaty confirming private rules made by exchanges or
                    commercial associations, either in Allied countries or in Italy.</p>
            </div>
